<title>DENMARK: Maersk, Sea-Land run South America route.</title>
<headline>Maersk, Sea-Land run South America route.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish energy and shipping group A.P. Moeller's Maersk Line said on Monday that it was cooperating with its U.S. partner Sea-Land in extending services between South America's east coast and North America.</p>
<p>On July 22, Maersk and Sea-Land announced cooperation on direct services linking ports in northern Europe with Montreal, Canada, along with P&amp;O Nedlloyd.</p>
<p>Maersk said that the earlier cooperation deal between itself and Sea-Land and Brazilian shipping company Transroll had been annulled. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen news service +45-33969652</p>
</text>
